{"questions":[{"question_id":"9BvtDiokWWAJbNgs","paperTitle":"AIEEE 2011","year":2011,"examDate":2011,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"periodic-table-and-periodicity","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","topic":"nature-of-oxide","type":"mcq","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"which-one-of-the-following-order-represents-the-correct-sequ-2011-marks-4-9bvtdiokwwajbngs.htm","content":"Which one of the following order represents the correct sequence of the increasing basic nature of the\ngiven oxides ?","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"MgO &lt; K<sub>2</sub>O &lt; Al<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub> &lt; Na<sub>2</sub>O"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Al<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub> &lt; MgO &lt; Na<sub>2</sub>O &lt; K<sub>2</sub>O"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Na<sub>2</sub>O &lt; K<sub>2</sub>O &lt; MgO &lt; Al<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub>"},{"identifier":"D","content":"K<sub>2</sub>O &lt; Na<sub>2</sub>O &lt; Al<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub> &lt; MgO"}],"correct_options":["B"],"explanation":"You should know that, \n<br><br>(1)<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.133ex\" height=\"0.036ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 0 501 16\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mspace\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mspace\" transform=\"translate(167,0)\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mspace\" transform=\"translate(334,0)\"></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> In a period, from left to right the acidic strength increases that mean basic nature decreases.\n<br><br>(2)<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.133ex\" height=\"0.036ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 0 501 16\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mspace\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mspace\" transform=\"translate(167,0)\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mspace\" transform=\"translate(334,0)\"></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> In a group, from top to bottom the basic nature increases that means acidic nature decreases. \n<br><br>Na, Mg,  Al and K are present in periodic table like this : -\n<br><br>\n<table class=\"tg\">\n  <tbody><tr>\n    <th class=\"tg-de48\"></th>\n    <th class=\"tg-de48\">Group 1</th>\n    <th class=\"tg-de48\">Group 2</th>\n    <th class=\"tg-de48\"></th>\n    <th class=\"tg-ujoh\">Group 13</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-de48\">Period 3</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-wv9z\">Na</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-wv9z\">Mg</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-wv9z\">.....</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-wrg0\">Al</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-de48\">Period 4</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-wv9z\">K</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-wv9z\"></td>\n    <td class=\"tg-wv9z\"></td>\n    <td class=\"tg-wrg0\"></td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<br><br>So, you can see Na,  Mg and Al are present in same period so the order of basic nature among Na, Mg and Al is Na &gt; Mg &gt; Al.\n<br><br>And Na and K are from same group so basic nature of K &gt; Na.\n<br><br>So the correct order of oxides \n<br><br>Al<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub> &lt; MgO &lt; Na<sub>2</sub>O &lt; K<sub>2</sub>O "}]}